60,3,1,talk,May,,Option B is a total non-starter for me. Who wants to wake up at dawn to stand around for an hour? And Option C just leaves the bins exactly where they've been for years. That's not fair.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,I agree with May. Option C is risky given the smell and maintenance issues I found at the station block. Option B is also impractical since people are unwilling to police each other's bags.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I'm with you! Option C is way too expensive, and I don't want anyone to struggle with the bill. Option B sounds like a lot of work for no reason. Option A seems much better!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Midori,,I agree that Option C is too risky and Option B is too demanding. Option A seems the most gentle approach; it shares the burden and ensures no one feels singled out or stuck with the nuisance forever.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Option A is a graceful choice. It avoids the heavy burden of supervision and the rigid constraints of a permanent build, allowing the responsibility to flow naturally among us without weighing anyone down.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,May,,"@Midori, exactly! If we just pick C, we're basically telling one neighbor ""thanks for hosting the trash for a decade, here's a box to keep it there."" That's not equality; that's just a fancy way of staying unfair.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@May, you've hit on a crucial point. Option A is the only one that addresses the spatial unfairness. Since we know people won't police each other, rotating the location is the most logical way to distribute the annoyance.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, exactly! Plus, Option A doesn't cost a huge amount of money to start. If we go with C, we're just adding a giant bill on top of everything else. Let's keep it simple and fair!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, I completely agree. If we can show that we're all willing to take a turn, it might help heal those old wounds. It's a way of saying we're all in this together as neighbors.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"Indeed, the act of sharing a burden is what transforms a group of residents into a true community. By rotating the location, we ensure that no one person is left to carry the weight of the neighborhood's needs alone.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,May,,I'm totally on board with Option A. It's the only one that actually moves the trash away from that one poor soul's gate. Let's stop pretending a box or a schedule makes it equal!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree. Option A is the most pragmatic choice. It avoids the financial risk of C and the social friction of B, while ensuring that the daily annoyance of the refuse point is shared equally among us.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm voting for A too! It's the cheapest option, it's fair for everyone's wallet, and it means we can all be friends without worrying about who's paying for what or who's stuck with the smell!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I'm voting for A as well. It feels like the kindest way to resolve this, as it shows we value each other's space equally and want to move forward in harmony.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"I shall also cast my vote for Option A. It is the most compassionate path, ensuring that the labor of our community remains light and that no single neighbor is worn down by a permanent burden.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,May,,It's settled then! Option A is the only way to actually make things fair. I'm voting for A—let's get those bins moving!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I'm voting for A. It's the most logical and compassionate solution, ensuring that no one is stuck with a permanent nuisance while avoiding the pitfalls of cost and conflict.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm voting for A! It's the best way to keep things fair and friendly for everyone, and it definitely won't break the bank. Let's do it!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Midori,,I'm voting for A. I truly hope this helps us all start fresh and brings back the friendly spirit of our lane.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"I cast my vote for Option A. May we all find peace in this shared effort, knowing that by lifting the burden from one, we strengthen the bond between us all.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
